# CCCI modem filesystem daemon, device-owned.
#
# Derived from stock /vendor/etc/init/init.cccifsd.rc. Same reason for owning it
# as init.cccimdinit.rc beside this file, and the same single difference: the
# MD3 half is gone, because this chassis has no C2K modem. See that file's
# header for the six measurements.
#
# `vendor.ccci3_fsd` was the worse of the two MD3 services. Unlike ccci3_mdinit
# it is not oneshot, so it did not exit: it opened /dev/ccci_md3_sta and parked
# in ccci_util_bc_read forever, waiting for a status broadcast from a modem that
# will never boot. Measured after 10 h of uptime it held one device fd and one
# socket, had accumulated 1 utime / 2 stime jiffies against the real instance's
# 28 / 86, and cost ~2.8 MB RSS for nothing.
#
# Keep `vendor.ccci_fsd` exactly as stock has it -- MD1 needs it, and its
# priority/ioprio lines are load-bearing for modem filesystem latency.

on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/vendor/ccci_cfg 0770 system radio
    restorecon /data/vendor/ccci_cfg
    mkdir /data/vendor/mdlpm 0770 system radio
    restorecon /data/vendor/mdlpm

    restorecon_recursive /mnt/vendor/protect_f
    restorecon_recursive /mnt/vendor/protect_s

service vendor.ccci_fsd /vendor/bin/ccci_fsd 0
    user radio
    group radio system root
    class core
    priority -20
    ioprio rt 4
    oneshot
